 D16 AND D17 timed modes both went solver_incomplete because the day's solver lacked the dispatch (D17 Mastery also needed the artifacts root set inside the per-set _solve_pairs worker). D17-night prebuild added equivalence/odd-one-out/thread groupings; non-hash ORDER keys are still open -> see synthesis-order-siblings. D18: Files = note + panel-001.png + installer-001.msi + video-001.mp4; the single worker pre-wired the dispatch -> TT 23 / Mastery 115 CORRECT in-window first try. D19: Files = note + document-001.pdf + shortcut-001.lnk + collector-001.elf; the single worker added an ELF extractor but NOT the synthesis branch -> TT and Mastery solver_incomplete -> offline generalize ported D18's branch. 4 of 5 timed days lost this way: the day's solver must start from the previous day's solve.py. D21: Files grew to FIVE names (note + panel png + managed dll + message eml + mobile-001.apk), same list in all 5 Mastery sets, order re-rolled per set -- never assume a count. D22-D23: Files = FIVE names and DIFFER between sets of one Mastery (D23: note/panel png/msi/mp4/sqlite vs note/pdf/lnk/mp4/sqlite) -- parse each set's text; still sha256-only. D24: FIVE names (note + document-001.pdf + collector-001.elf + shortcut-001.lnk + events-001.evtx), same five in all 8 Mastery sets, order re-rolled; sha256 only. D25: still sha256 order over 5 names (note/pdf/elf/lnk/hiv, or note/macos/docx/zip/hiv), per-set lists differ. D26: still sha256 + FIVE names (note + {evidence-drop-001.zip | document-001.pdf} + document-15-001.docx + macos-001.bin + trace-001.pf), pdf/zip swapped between Mastery sets; Mastery identity ids also differ per set (7 of 21 asked).\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"timed-carryover-mutations\", \"concept\": \"Timed kits mutate every carried family; json lists must be SORTED\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23 TT/Mastery re-rolled values that were constant D13-D22: PE Machine 0x01c0/0x01c2/0x01c4/0x01f0/0x0ebc/0x5064/0x8664, ELF e_machine 0x0003/0x0028/0x002b/0x0102, audio mp3/opus/vorbis/pcm_s16le, video dims arbitrary, Mach-O FAT 2-3 slices (0x7, 0xc, 0x12, 0x01000007, 0x0100000c, 0x01000012, 0x0200000c), shuffled zip CD, PDF 1.0-2.0, BOM true, identity sizes 72-378 B, sqlite page 512-65536. lib answered all values right; the two failures were list ORDER: GM wants zip CD names and macho cpu_type_set SORTED ascending (CD order rejected; fat_arch order != accepted) and a local override returned a Python list -> repr. Action for lib/solver owners: one json choke point (sorted + compact) for every `json` answer except `*-synthesis-*-order`; fixture tests with multi-slice fat, shuffled CD, Ogg Opus/Vorbis, MP3, non-x86 PE/ELF so the next carried family (sqlite) is covered for its mutations too (page size 1 = 65536, WAL header, UTF-16 encodings). D24: the D23 fixes held -- TT 29 / Mastery 232 (8 sets) first try while the kit mutated again: audio `ftyp M4A ` -> aac and `fLaC` -> flac (still named audio-001.wav), Mach-O thin LE-32 `ce fa ed fe` (60 B) -> [\\\"0x0000000c\\\"] beside fat 2-3 slices, PE 0x0266 MIPS16, ELF 0x0016 S390 / 0x00b7 AArch64 / 0x00f3 RISC-V, SQLite page 2048, PDF 1.1/1.6/1.7. Expect EVTX to mutate from D25: several chunks, record-id gaps, a dirty header, an empty or zeroed second chunk -- the record_count walk must cover every chunk. D25 (TT 30 / Mastery 270 = 9 sets) all first try with zero generalize: carried extractors held; identity names carry a random `-<6hex>` suffix (ids keep the bare stem), 2 of 9 Mastery sets used a different kit (macos/docx/inner zip, no roster). From D26 the kit carries `d25-registry-001-registry-hive-root-name`: parse root offset @0x24 generally (root not at 0x20, multiple hbins, UTF-16 name when nk flag 0x20 is clear, non-ASCII latin-1 names). D26: TT 31 / Mastery 310 (10 sets) first try; the NEW family's wrapper flipped between modes (single MAM\\\\x04-compressed prefetch, every timed .pf plain SCCA v30) -- branch on magic, never on mode. Expect D27+ timed kits to mutate prefetch (other SCCA versions 17/23/26/31, MAM with CRC, compressed in timed) and registry (root cell not @0x20, UTF-16 root names) -- see prefetch-carryover-variants.\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"gate-allowlist-dfir-libs\", \"concept\": \"Prebuild gate refuses installed DFIR libs\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS lacks Evtx, regipy, olefile, oletools, dnfile, LnkParse3, lief, cryptography, asn1crypto, dpkt, PIL, sqlite3, wave, ordlookup. Targets evtx-records (python-evtx) and regf-values (regipy) as written will fail the gate exactly like pe-debug-rich-imports did (import ordlookup). Either widen the allowlist (all are in .venv) or rewrite those goals as stdlib/struct parsers. Also `open` is banned: regipy RegistryHive needs a path -> use a struct nk/vk walker.\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"x509-cert\", \"concept\": \"X.509 subject/issuer/serial/validity/fingerprint\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt x509 (alias cert), fields subject_cn, issuer_cn, serial_hex, not_before_utc, not_after_utc, sha256_fingerprint, sha1_fingerprint, san_dns_names. Shares the DER walker with pe-authenticode; cryptography needs the allowlist.\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"windows-text-dfir-artifacts\", \"concept\": \"Text-shaped Windows DFIR artifacts: WER Report.wer, Defender MPLog / DetectionHistory / quarantine, PSReadLine history, setupapi.dev.log\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt wer (aliases report_wer, windows_error_report): UTF-16LE (BOM) INI-like `Key=Value` lines: Version, EventType (APPCRASH, BEX64, ...), EventTime (decimal FILETIME -> ISO Z), ReportIdentifier/IntegratorReportIdentifier (GUID verbatim), AppSessionGuid, Sig[N].Name/Sig[N].Value (Application Name, Application Version, Fault Module Name, Exception Code `c0000005`), NsAppName, AppName, AppPath, OriginalFilename, TargetAppId -> fields by key name snake_cased (app_name, app_path, event_type, fault_module_name, exception_code). fmt defender (aliases mplog, windows_defender): MPLog-*.log lines (`Threat`/`DETECTION`/`SDN` events, ThreatName, file paths after `file:`), DetectionHistory binary (GUID-named files, UTF-16 strings: threat name, resource path, process), quarantine `Entries\\\\{GUID}` + `ResourceData` RC4-encrypted with the well-known 256-byte Defender key (public in the defender-dump / dissect sources) -> detection_name, original_path, detection_time_utc. fmt psreadline (aliases consolehost_history, powershell_history): ConsoleHost_history.txt lines (backtick continuations) -> command_count, last_command, first_command, commands_matching (URL/download cradle). fmt setupapi (setupapi.dev.log): `>>>  [Device Install (Hardware initiated) - USBSTOR\\\\Disk&Ven_...]` + `>>>  Section start YYYY/MM/DD HH:MM:SS.mmm` -> usb_device_ids (sorted), first_install_time per device (local time, verbatim). No csv module (gate).\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"linux-dfir-logs\", \"concept\": \"Linux DFIR binaries: systemd journal files, utmp/wtmp/btmp, lastlog\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"A plausible post-Windows DFIR turn (host identity = machine id). fmt journald (aliases journal, systemd_journal): signature `LPKSHHRH` @0, compatible_flags u32 @8, incompatible_flags u32 @12 (bit0 XZ, bit1 LZ4, bit2 keyed hash, bit3 ZSTD, bit4 compact), state u8 @16 (0 offline, 1 online, 2 archived), file_id @24, machine_id @40 (16 B -> 32 lowercase hex, the 'host'), tail_entry_boot_id @56, seqnum_id @72, header_size u64 @88, arena_size u64 @96; counters (n_objects, n_entries, head/tail entry seqnum, head/tail entry realtime in us since 1970 -> ISO Z) follow per the systemd JOURNAL_FILE_FORMAT doc -- read their offsets from the doc, gate them on header_size. fmt utmp (aliases wtmp, btmp): 384-B records (glibc x86-64): ut_type i16 @0 (1 RUN_LVL, 2 BOOT_TIME, 5 INIT, 6 LOGIN, 7 USER_PROCESS, 8 DEAD_PROCESS), pid i32 @4, line 32 B @8, id 4 B @40, user 32 B @44, host 256 B @76, exit @332, session i32 @336, tv_sec i32 @340, tv_usec @344, addr_v6 16 B @348 -> record_count, user_names (sorted unique), hosts, boot_count, first/last login time, logins_for_<user>. fmt lastlog: 292-B records indexed by UID {time i32, line 32 B, host 256 B}.\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"pcap-header\", \"concept\": \"PCAP/PCAPNG global header, linktype, packet count, interfaces\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt pcap / pcapng, fields magic_u32_hex, version, linktype, snaplen, packet_count, first_packet_time_utc, if_names (pcapng IDB if_name option 2), shb_os. Pure struct.\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"memory-image-headers\", \"concept\": \"Memory acquisition formats beyond Windows crash dumps: LiME, AVML, VMware vmss/vmsn/vmem, VirtualBox core\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"crash-memory-dump-headers (built) covers MDMP / PAGEDU64 / hiberfil. fmt lime (aliases memory_image): range headers magic 0x4C694D45 (`EMiL` on disk) u32 @0, version u32 @4 (1), start u64 @8, end u64 @16 (inclusive), reserved 8 B, then (end-start+1) bytes -> range_count (walk), total_size_bytes, first_range_start_hex, ranges (JSON `0x%x-0x%x`). fmt avml: `AVML` magic + version u32 + start/end u64 + snappy-framed blocks (header only). fmt vmware_state (vmss/vmsn): magic u32 0xbed2bed0 / 0xbad1bad1 / 0xbed3bed3, group count u32 @8, 80-B group entries {name 64 B, offset u64, size u64} -> group_names (file order), has_memory_group. VirtualBox `VBCORE` ELF core note. A raw `.vmem`/`.raw` has no header -> only identity fields.\"}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ec1e2bbe-ac7e-4c42-acc0-4fae81d05a35","uuid":"0b833681-54d8-44b4-a0ff-48f545f07602","timestamp":"2026-10-27T13:09:02.979Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"(\"pcapng\", \"application\") (\"pcapng\", \"block_count\") (\"pcapng\", \"block_type_u32_hex\") (\"pcapng\", \"byte_order_magic_u32_hex\") (\"pcapng\", \"capture_application\") (\"pcapng\", \"capture_comment\") (\"pcapng\", \"capture_end_time_utc\") (\"pcapng\", \"cap