{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSo7fdf4wmDos6Wxfrh6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SK6uLm25rR1b1DbURDU9x9","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; cat > $TMPDIR/ed_cov.py <<'PYEOF'\nimport json\np='reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md'\nt=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global t\n    assert t.count(a)==1,(t.count(a),a[:70]); t=t.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"(as of D26 post-run, 2026-10-26)\",\"(as of D27 post-run, 2026-10-27)\")\nrep(\"\"\"Progression: D19-D22 runnable formats -> D23 APPLICATION DATA -> D24-D26 WINDOWS DFIR (EVTX walk, hive pointer-follow,\nprefetch decompress-then-parse), fmt = the DOMAIN word, one artifact per day, every family lasting one day. D27-D29\nmost plausibly more of the DFIR block:\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**D27 \"Packet Loss Prevention\" = PCAP** (`pcap.packet_count` of one `capture-001.pcap`, 119 B: classic libpcap LE-us\n`d4 c3 b2 a1` v2.4, snaplen 65535, linktype 147 USER0, 3 records; id `d27-pcap-001-pcap-packet-count`, `integer`/\n`trim`). Count = 24-B global header, then 16-B record headers advancing by incl_len u32 @+8 until EOF. The D16-night\nprebuild `pcap.py` HIT the race (CORRECT ~22 s, 0 wrong); TT 32 / Mastery 352 (ELEVEN sets, 5.8 s) first try. Timed\npcaps mutated inside the classic format only: magic LE-us / LE-ns `4d 3c b2 a1` / BE-us `a1 b2 c3 d4` (3 of 11 sets\nbig-endian), linktype 1/101/105/147, snaplen 256-262144, 3-39 records, some snapped (incl_len < orig_len, still\ncounted); no pcapng, no truncated tail. Synthesis grew to SIX names (note/png/msi/wav/jar/pcap). Flavor (unasked):\n\"Packet captures, exports, and host artifacts describe the same incident from different angles. Count traffic,\nreject malformed captures, and find the host narrative missing network evidence.\" -> siblings: malformed-capture\ndetection (truncated record, incl_len > snaplen, bad version), flow/log EXPORTS (Zeek, NetFlow, CSV) whose count\ndiffers, HOST artifacts (Sysmon EID 3/22, firewall log, netstat) claiming a connection the capture lacks.\nProgression: D19-D22 runnable formats -> D23 APPLICATION DATA -> D24-D26 WINDOWS DFIR (EVTX walk, hive pointer-follow,\nprefetch decompress-then-parse) -> D27 NETWORK (pcap record walk), fmt = the file-format/DOMAIN word, one artifact per\nday, every family lasting one day. D28-D31 (four days left): the D27 flavor names \"exports\" and \"host artifacts\" ->\nmost plausible next = a network EXPORT format (pcapng / Zeek / NetFlow / HAR) or host network evidence, else a\nreturn to unbuilt DFIR (WER/Defender/PSReadLine, Linux journald/utmp) or cloud/identity audit logs (M365 UAL,\nCloudTrail -- on-brand for Huntress ITDR). Older DFIR forecast (still valid, mostly built):\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"Carried families keep mutating in the timed kits; expect the prefetch wrapper/version to flip (D26 already flipped\ncompressed -> plain between modes): keep extractors general (all SCCA versions, MAM with/without CRC).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Carried families keep mutating in the timed kits; expect the prefetch wrapper/version to flip (D26 already flipped\ncompressed -> plain between modes) and the pcap container to flip (pcapng / Kuznetzov / truncated tail from D28):\nkeep extractors general (all SCCA versions, MAM with/without CRC; every pcap magic + pcapng EPB/SPB/OPB).\"\"\")\n# atlas rows\ni=t.index(\"| 78 | PCAP/PCAPNG header\"); j=t.index(\"\\n\",i)\nt=t[:i]+\"| 78 | PCAP/PCAPNG header: magic/endianness, linktype, snaplen, packet count, IDB if_name, SHB hardware/OS | seen D27 `pcap.packet_count` (complete classic records walked; LE-us/LE-ns/BE magics, linktypes 1/101/105/147 in timed); rest prebuilt pcap (speculative); malformed/carry-over = gap (pcap-malformed-integrity, pcap-carryover-variants) | `d4 c3 b2 a1`/`4d 3c b2 a1` (ns)/`a1 b2 c3 d4` BE; `0a 0d 0d 0a` | struct; `lib/meta/prebuilt/pcap.py`; `capinfos -M` (I); dpkt (I, worker-only) | high (carry-over every timed kit from D28) |\"+t[j:]\ni=t.index(\"| 79 | PCAP content\"); j=t.index(\"\\n\",i)\nt=t[:i]+\"| 79 | PCAP content: L3/L4 (unique IPs, conversations, ports, protocol counts, bytes) and app indicators (DNS qnames, HTTP Host/UA/URI, TLS SNI) | gap (pcap-l3l4-decode, pcap-app-indicators) | as #78; decode per linktype (1 Ethernet, 101 raw IP, 113/276 SLL, 0 NULL) | `tshark -r f -T fields -e dns.qry.name` (I); dpkt (I, worker-only); struct in-window | high (D27 flavor: \\\"count traffic\\\") |\"+t[j:]\ni=t.index(\"| 174 | Memory images\"); j=t.index(\"\\n\",i)\nt=t[:j]+\"\"\"\n| 175 | Malformed captures: truncated tail record, incl_len > snaplen / > orig_len, bad version, pcapng block-length mismatch; \"which capture is malformed\" | gap (pcap-malformed-integrity) | record walk ends short of EOF; trailing bytes | struct | high (D27 flavor \"reject malformed captures\") |\n| 176 | Network EXPORTS: Zeek TSV/JSON logs, Suricata eve.json, NetFlow v5/v9/IPFIX, Wireshark CSV, W3C firewall logs (`pfirewall.log`) | gap (network-flow-log-exports) | `#separator \\\\x09` + `#fields`; `\"event_type\":`; u16 version 5/9/10 @0; `#Fields:` | stdlib text/struct | high (D27 flavor \"exports\") |\n| 177 | Host network evidence: Sysmon EID 3 NetworkConnect / 22 DNSEvent, netstat/ipconfig text, hosts file, DNS cache; host-claim vs capture join | gap (host-network-evidence, host-vs-network-synthesis) | EVTX Sysmon channel; `Proto  Local Address` header | evtx_binxml (built) + text parsers | high (D27 flavor \"host narrative missing network evidence\") |\n| 178 | Capture-format zoo: snoop, NetMon `GMBU`, ERF, Kuznetzov `a1b2cd34`, pktmon/netsh `.etl`, gz-wrapped pcap; HAR JSON | gap (capture-format-zoo, har-json-capture) | `snoop\\\\0\\\\0\\\\0`; `GMBU`; `{\"log\":{\"version\"` | struct / json | med |\n| 179 | Cloud / identity audit logs: M365 Unified Audit Log CSV/JSON, Entra sign-ins, AWS CloudTrail `Records[]`, Okta System Log | gap (cloud-identity-audit-logs) | `\"eventVersion\"`+`\"eventSource\"`; `CreationDate,UserIds,Operations,AuditData` | json / csv text | low-med (Huntress ITDR theme) |\"\"\"+t[j:]\n# cue line\nold=\"d4 c3 b2 a1 / a1 b2 c3 d4 / 0a 0d 0d 0a  PCAP/PCAPNG  linktype u32 @20; capinfos -M; dpkt\"\nnew=\"d4 c3 b2 a1 LE-us / 4d 3c b2 a1 LE-ns / a1 b2 c3 d4 BE / 0a 0d 0d 0a pcapng: PCAP (D27 `pcap.packet_count` = walk 16-B rec hdrs by incl_len@+8 from 24; order FROM MAGIC; snapped recs count); pcapng EPB6/SPB3/OPB2\"\nrep(old,new)\n# gaps\ni=t.index('## Readiness gaps'); j=t.index('```json',i); k=t.index('```',j+7)\ng=json.loads(t[j+7:k])\ng=[x for x in g if x['id']!='pcap-header']\nby={x['id']:x for x in g}\nby['synthesis-siblings']['detail']+=\" D27: SIX names (note/png/msi/wav/jar/pcap, order shuffled per set) in TT and all 11 Mastery sets, still sha256 -- the list length grows; parse it, never count it.\"\nby['timed-carryover-mutations']['detail']+=\" D27: TT 32 / Mastery 352 (11 sets) first try with zero generalize; the new pcap family already mutated within classic libpcap in the timed sets (LE-us, LE-ns 4d3cb2a1, BE a1b2c3d4; linktypes 1/101/105/147; snapped records). From D28 the kit carries d27-pcap-001-pcap-packet-count -- see pcap-carryover-variants.\"\nfor x in g:\n    if x['id'] in ('ese-edb-header','amcache-shimcache','usn-journal-records','recycle-bin-i','jumplist','mft-record','ntfs-boot-sector-vbr'):\n        x['priority']=2\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"pcap-carryover-variants\",\"concept\":\"PCAP as a CARRIED timed family: every container the D28+ kits may mutate capture-001.pcap into\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Harden lib/meta/prebuilt/pcap.py packet_count (and every pcap field) for: pcapng (SHB 0a0d0d0a with BOM 1a2b3c4d either order, MULTIPLE sections each re-setting byte order, count EPB 6 + SPB 3 + obsolete PB 2 only -- not IDB/ISB/NRB/DSB/custom 0x0bad/0x40000bad), Kuznetzov modified pcap magic a1b2cd34 (24-B record header: +ifindex u32, protocol u16, pkt_type u8, pad), nanosecond a1b23c4d in both orders, IXIA/AIX variants (a1b2c3d4 with version 2.2/2.3), a truncated tail record (not counted, capinfos behaviour), zero-length records (counted), gzip-wrapped `.pcap.gz` (1f 8b -> decompress then parse). Fixtures: each magic x each byte order, pcapng with 2 sections + 2 IDBs, a 1-byte-short tail. Fields stay packet_count / linktype / snaplen / first/last_packet_time_utc.\"},\n {\"id\":\"pcap-malformed-integrity\",\"concept\":\"Malformed-capture detection ('reject malformed captures', D27 flavor)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"New module lib/meta/prebuilt/pcap_integrity.py (pure struct, reuse pcap.py parse). fmt pcap/pcapng fields: is_malformed / is_valid (enum true|false), malformed_reason (enum-ish: truncated_record, incl_len_exceeds_snaplen, incl_len_exceeds_orig_len, bad_magic, bad_version, block_length_mismatch, trailing_bytes), truncated_record_count, trailing_bytes_count (bytes after the last complete record), complete_record_count, declared_vs_walked mismatch for pcapng ISB isb_ifrecv/isb_ifdrop, records_exceeding_snaplen_count, non_monotonic_timestamp_count, max_incl_len. Synthesis shapes: '*-malformed-capture-names' / 'which of Files is malformed' -> JSON sorted list of member names whose walk fails; 'valid capture count'. Never raise: a malformed file must still answer packet_count = complete records.\"},\n {\"id\":\"pcap-l3l4-decode\",\"concept\":\"Packet decode L2-L4: unique IPs, conversations, ports, protocol counts, byte totals\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"New module lib/meta/prebuilt/pcap_flows.py (stdlib struct only; dpkt is not gate-allowed). Decode per linktype: 1 Ethernet (+802.1Q/QinQ 8100/88a8, ethertype 0800/86dd/0806), 0 NULL/BSD loopback (u32 AF host order), 101/12/14 raw IP, 113 Linux SLL (16 B), 276 SLL2 (20 B), 105 802.11 + 127 radiotap (LLC/SNAP), 228/229 raw IPv4/IPv6; skip 147-162 USER* (count only). IPv4 IHL, IPv6 next-header chain, TCP data offset, UDP. Fields (fmt pcap, also pcapng): unique_ip_count, unique_src_ips / unique_dst_ips (sorted JSON), top_talker_ip (most packets, tie -> lowest), conversation_count (unordered IP pair) and flow_count (5-tuple, unordered), tcp_packet_count, udp_packet_count, icmp_packet_count, arp_packet_count, ipv6_packet_count, protocol_counts (JSON object?), dst_ports (sorted ints), total_bytes (sum orig_len) vs captured_bytes (sum incl_len), tcp_syn_count, capture_duration_seconds, most_common_dst_port. Spellings: IPs dotted / RFC 5952 compressed IPv6 lowercase.\"},\n {\"id\":\"pcap-app-indicators\",\"concept\":\"Application-layer indicators from captures: DNS, HTTP, TLS SNI, FTP/SMTP creds\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Builds on pcap-l3l4-decode (import its walker). DNS over UDP/53 (and TCP/53 length-prefixed): query names (label decode with compression pointers, lowercase, no trailing dot), qtypes, answer A/AAAA/CNAME values, rcode NXDOMAIN count -> dns_query_names (sorted unique JSON), dns_answer_ips, most_queried_domain. HTTP/1.x on any TCP payload starting with a method token: methods, Host, request URIs, User-Agent, response status codes, Content-Type; first request URL = http://Host+URI. TLS: ClientHello (handshake type 1) SNI extension 0, ALPN 16, version; Certificate (TLS<=1.2) DER -> hand to x509 module (sha256 fingerprint, subject CN). Optional JA3 (md5 of version,ciphers,extensions,curves,formats; GREASE removed). FTP USER/PASS, SMTP MAIL FROM/RCPT TO, ICMP payload strings. Fields: dns_query_names, http_hosts, http_user_agents, http_request_uris, tls_sni_names, tls_ja3_md5, ftp_usernames, smtp_mail_from -- all lists sorted+deduped; *_first / *_count variants.\"},\n {\"id\":\"network-flow-log-exports\",\"concept\":\"Network EXPORTS beside a capture: Zeek, Suricata eve.json, NetFlow v5/v9/IPFIX, Wireshark CSV, W3C firewall logs\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D27 flavor: 'Packet captures, exports, and host artifacts'. New module lib/meta/prebuilt/netlogs.py (stdlib, no csv module if gate forbids -> manual split). fmt zeek (aliases bro, conn_log, dns_log, http_log): TSV with `#separator \\\\x09`, `#fields` and `#types` headers, `#close`; or JSON-lines -> record_count, unique uids, id.orig_h/id.resp_h sets, service set, total orig_bytes/resp_bytes, dns query set, http host set. fmt suricata (eve, eve_json): JSON lines event_type alert/dns/http/tls/flow -> alert_signatures (sorted), alert_count, signature_ids, src/dest ips. fmt netflow: v5 header (version u16 BE =5 @0, count u16 @2, sys_uptime, unix_secs @8) + 48-B records (srcaddr, dstaddr, nexthop, input, output, dPkts, dOctets, first, last, srcport, dstport, tcp_flags, prot) -> record_count, total_packets (sum dPkts), total_bytes, unique dst; v9/IPFIX (version 9/10) template flowsets -> record_count via templates. fmt csv_flows (Wireshark 'Export Packet Dissections as CSV': \\\"No.\\\",\\\"Time\\\",\\\"Source\\\",\\\"Destination\\\",\\\"Protocol\\\",\\\"Length\\\",\\\"Info\\\") -> row_count, protocols. fmt firewall_log (pfirewall.log W3C `#Fields: date time action protocol src-ip dst-ip src-port dst-port size ...`) -> drop_count, allow_count, unique dst. Cross-check field: export count vs capture packet_count disagreement.\"},\n {\"id\":\"host-network-evidence\",\"concept\":\"Host artifacts that narrate network activity: Sysmon EID 3/22, netstat/ipconfig text, hosts file, DNS client cache, RDP/VPN logs\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D27 flavor: 'find the host narrative missing network evidence'. New module lib/meta/prebuilt/host_net.py. EVTX path: reuse evtx_binxml (built) to read Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational EID 3 (Image, Protocol, SourceIp, SourcePort, DestinationIp, DestinationHostname, DestinationPort, UtcTime) and EID 22 (QueryName, QueryResults, Image); Security 5156 WFP (Application, DestAddress, DestPort); TerminalServices 1149 (source IP). Text paths: `netstat -ano` (Proto Local Address Foreign Address State PID) -> established remote endpoints; `ipconfig /displaydns` (Record Name / A (Host) Record); hosts file non-comment mappings; bash/zsh history ssh/curl/wget/nc targets. Fields: remote_ips (sorted), remote_endpoints (`ip:port` sorted), dns_query_names, connecting_images (process paths), connection_count, first_connection_time_utc.\"},\n {\"id\":\"host-vs-network-synthesis\",\"concept\":\"Cross-member join: host claims vs capture traffic (the claim with no matching packets)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"New lib/meta/prebuilt/synthesis_network.py using pcap-l3l4-decode + host-network-evidence + network-flow-log-exports. Given Files [capture(s), host logs, exports]: build the capture's (dst ip, dst port, proto) set and DNS names; for each host claim (Sysmon EID3 / netstat / firewall allow / Zeek conn row) test presence -> answers: host_claims_missing_network_evidence (JSON sorted `ip:port` or member name of the host artifact whose narrative has no packets), capture_without_host_evidence, matched_claim_count, the HOSTNAME/member that lies. Also 'which capture is malformed' (via pcap-malformed-integrity) and 'total packets across valid captures'. Id guess: metadata-day-NN-synthesis-<what> or dNN-<fmt>-NNN-...-missing-*; dispatch on any id containing missing|unmatched|without|orphan.\"},\n {\"id\":\"capture-format-zoo\",\"concept\":\"Non-libpcap capture formats and wrappers: snoop, NetMon, ERF, pktmon/netsh ETL, gz-wrapped\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Extend pcap packet_count/linktype to: Solaris snoop (`snoop\\\\0\\\\0\\\\0` @0, version u32 BE @8, datalink u32 @12; records orig_len u32, incl_len u32, record_len u32 (padded), drops, ts sec/usec -> walk by record_len), Microsoft Network Monitor 2.x (`GMBU` @0, ver @4/@5, mac type u16 @6, frame table offset u32 @0x18 / length @0x1c -> frame count = len/4), NetMon 1.x (`RTSS`), Endace ERF (no magic: 16-B record hdr ts u64, type u8, flags, rlen u16 BE, lctr, wlen -> walk by rlen), pcap-in-gzip (1f 8b), Windows pktmon/netsh trace .etl (event count via the built etl module; pktmon PacketFragment events). fmt words pcap/capture/snoop/netmon/erf. An unknown magic -> 'none' (do not guess a count).\"},\n {\"id\":\"har-json-capture\",\"concept\":\"HAR 1.2 HTTP archive exports (browser 'save as HAR')\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"fmt har: JSON {log:{version, creator{name,version}, browser, pages[], entries[]}} -> entry_count, page_count, creator_name, creator_version, request_urls (sorted unique), request_methods, response_status_codes, server_ip_addresses (entries[].serverIPAddress), first_request_url (by startedDateTime ISO), hosts (from URL netloc), mime types, total response bodySize (skip -1), cookies names. Web lane overlaps (it also parses HAR) -- keep pure json/urllib.parse.\"},\n {\"id\":\"tls-certs-in-capture\",\"concept\":\"Certificates and TLS fingerprints carried inside captures; SSLKEYLOGFILE\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"From pcap-app-indicators TLS reassembly (TCP segments of one stream in seq order): Certificate handshake (type 11, TLS<=1.2) -> leaf DER -> reuse prebuilt x509 (subject_cn, issuer_cn, serial_hex, not_after_utc, sha256_fingerprint); server_cert_fingerprints (sorted); JA3/JA3S md5; ServerHello chosen cipher hex `0x%04x`. fmt sslkeylog (text `CLIENT_RANDOM <64 hex> <96 hex>` / TLS1.3 `CLIENT_HANDSHAKE_TRAFFIC_SECRET`) -> line_count, client_randoms, label set; pcapng DSB (block type 0x0000000A, secrets type 0x544c534b 'TLSK') -> embedded keylog.\"},\n {\"id\":\"cloud-identity-audit-logs\",\"concept\":\"Cloud / identity audit exports: M365 Unified Audit Log, Entra sign-in logs, AWS CloudTrail, Okta System Log\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"On-brand for Huntress ITDR; plausible 'host/identity narrative' artifact in the last days. fmt ual (aliases m365_audit, unified_audit_log): CSV CreationDate,UserIds,Operations,AuditData(JSON string) -> record_count, operations (sorted unique), user_ids, client_ips (AuditData.ClientIP / ActorIpAddress), first/last CreationDate; MailItemsAccessed / New-InboxRule names. fmt entra_signin (JSON array or CSV): userPrincipalName, ipAddress, appDisplayName, status.errorCode, location -> failed_signin_count, ip set. fmt cloudtrail: {\\\"Records\\\":[{eventVersion,eventTime,eventSource,eventName,awsRegion,sourceIPAddress,userIdentity{type,arn,userName}}]} (also gz) -> record_count, event_names (sorted unique), source_ips, regions, first_event_time_utc. fmt okta (System Log JSON: eventType, actor.alternateId, client.ipAddress, outcome.result). Pure json; manual CSV split honouring quotes.\"},\n]\ng.extend(new)\norder={1:0,2:1,3:2}\ng.sort(key=lambda x:x['priority'])  # stable within priority\nblob=\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False) for x in g)+\"\\n]\"\njson.loads(blob)\nt=t[:j+7]+\"\\n\"+blob+\"\\n\"+t[k:]\n# ranking prose\na=t.index(\"Ranking (D26 post-run)\"); b=t.index(\"TARGETS-style `fmt`/`fields` given in `detail`\")\nt=t[:a]+\"\"\"Ranking (D27 post-run): priority 1 = plausible D28-D30 question with no extractor or a lane-wide failure mode.\nD27 left the WINDOWS DFIR block (D24-26) for NETWORK evidence (`pcap.packet_count`, fmt = file-format word). Its flavor\nnames three angles -- captures, EXPORTS, HOST artifacts -- plus \"reject malformed captures\" and \"host narrative\nmissing network evidence\", so priority 1 = making the newly carried pcap family survive timed mutation (pcapng,\nKuznetzov, truncated tail), malformed-capture detection, packet decode (flows, DNS/HTTP/TLS), flow-log exports\n(Zeek/Suricata/NetFlow/firewall) and host network evidence + the host-vs-capture join. Unbuilt Windows text DFIR,\nLinux DFIR, HAR, capture-format zoo and cloud/identity audit logs at 2; certs-in-capture at 3. The built D24-26 DFIR\npriority-1 items moved to 2 (built; the prebuild drains only unbuilt `prebuild` gaps).\n\"\"\"+t[b:]\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\nPYEOF\npython3 $TMPDIR/ed_cov.py && echo ok"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3589,"cache_read_input_tokens":102380,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3589},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ec1e2bbe-ac7e-4c42-acc0-4fae81d05a35","uuid":"156fdf3c-cb4e-4366-bb0b-0bc19913c7ef","timestamp":"2026-10-27T13:10:52.971Z","request_id":"req_011CgSo7fEcADco5HQwHcrGf","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01SK6uLm25rR1b1DbURDU9x9":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; cat > $TMPDIR/ed_cov.py <<'PYEOF'\nimport json\np='reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md'\nt=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global t\n    assert t.count(a)==1,(t.count(a),a[:70]); t=t.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"(as of D26 post-run, 2026-10-26)\",\"(as of D27 post-run, 2026-10-27)\")\nrep(\"\"\"Progression: D19-D22 runnable formats -> D23 APPLICATION DATA -> D24-D26 WINDOWS DFIR (EVTX walk, hive pointer-follow,\nprefetch decompress-then-parse), fmt = the DOMAIN word, one artifact per day, every family lasting one day. D27-D29\nmost plausibly more of the DFIR block:\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**D27 \"Packet Loss Prevention\" = PCAP** (`pcap.packet_count` of one `capture-001.pcap`, 119 B: classic libpcap LE-us\n`d4 c3 b2 a1` v2.4, snaplen 65535, linktype 147 USER0, 3 records; id `d27-pcap-001-pcap-packet-count`, `integer`/\n`trim`). Count = 24-B global header, then 16-B record headers advancing by incl_len u32 @+8 until EOF. The D16-night\nprebuild `pcap.py` HIT the race (CORRECT ~22 s, 0 wrong); TT 32 / Mastery 352 (ELEVEN sets, 5.8 s) first try. Timed\npcaps mutated inside the classic format only: magic LE-us / LE-ns `4d 3c b2 a1` / BE-us `a1 b2 c3 d4` (3 of 11 sets\nbig-endian), linktype 1/101/105/147, snaplen 256-262144, 3-39 records, some snapped (incl_len < orig_len, still\ncounted); no pcapng, no truncated tail. Synthesis grew to SIX names (note/png/msi/wav/jar/pcap). Flavor (unasked):\n\"Packet captures, exports, and host artifacts describe the same incident from different angles. Count traffic,\nreject malformed captures, and find the host narrative missing network evidence.\" -> siblings: malformed-capture\ndetection (truncated record, incl_len > snaplen, bad version), flow/log EXPORTS (Zeek, NetFlow, CSV) whose count\ndiffers, HOST artifacts (Sysmon EID 3/22, firewall log, netstat) claiming a connection the capture lacks.\nProgression: D19-D22 runnable formats -> D23 APPLICATION DATA -> D24-D26 WINDOWS DFIR (EVTX walk, hive pointer-follow,\nprefetch decompress-then-parse) -> D27 NETWORK (pcap record walk), fmt = the file-format/DOMAIN word, one artifact per\nday, every family lasting one day. D28-D31 (four days left): the D27 flavor names \"exports\" and \"host artifacts\" ->\nmost plausible next = a network EXPORT format (pcapng / Zeek / NetFlow / HAR) or host network evidence, else a\nreturn to unbuilt DFIR (WER/Defender/PSReadLine, Linux journald/utmp) or cloud/identity audit logs (M365 UAL,\nCloudTrail -- on-brand for Huntress ITDR). Older DFIR forecast (still valid, mostly built):\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"Carried families keep mutating in the timed kits; expect the prefetch wrapper/version to flip (D26 already flipped\ncompressed -> plain between modes): keep extractors general (all SCCA versions, MAM with/without CRC).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Carried families keep mutating in the timed kits; expect the prefetch wrapper/version to flip (D26 already flipped\ncompressed -> plain between modes) and the pcap container to flip (pcapng / Kuznetzov / truncated tail from D28):\nkeep extractors general (all SCCA versions, MAM with/without CRC; every pcap magic + pcapng EPB/SPB/OPB).\"\"\")\n# atlas rows\ni=t.index(\"| 78 | PCAP/PCAPNG header\"); j=t.index(\"\\n\",i)\nt=t[:i]+\"| 78 | PCAP/PCAPNG header: magic/endianness, linktype, snaplen, packet count, IDB if_name, SHB hardware/OS | seen D27 `pcap.packet_count` (complete classic records walked; LE-us/LE-ns/BE magics, linktypes 1/101/105/147 in timed); rest prebuilt pcap (speculative); malformed/carry-over = gap (pcap-malformed-integrity, pcap-carryover-variants) | `d4 c3 b2 a1`/`4d 3c b2 a1` (ns)/`a1 b2 c3 d4` BE; `0a 0d 0d 0a` | struct; `lib/meta/prebuilt/pcap.py`; `capinfos -M` (I); dpkt (I, worker-only) | high (carry-over every timed kit from D28) |\"+t[j:]\ni=t.index(\"| 79 | PCAP content\"); j=t.index(\"\\n\",i)\nt=t[:i]+\"| 79 | PCAP content: L3/L4 (unique IPs, conversations, ports, protocol counts, bytes) and app indicators (DNS qnames, HTTP Host/UA/URI, TLS SNI) | gap (pcap-l3l4-decode, pcap-app-indicators) | as #78; decode per linktype (1 Ethernet, 101 raw IP, 113/276 SLL, 0 NULL) | `tshark -r f -T fields -e dns.qry.name` (I); dpkt (I, worker-only); struct in-window | high (D27 flavor: \\\"count traffic\\\") |\"+t[j:]\ni=t.index(\"| 174 | Memory images\"); j=t.index(\"\\n\",i)\nt=t[:j]+\"\"\"\n| 175 | Malformed captures: truncated tail record, incl_len > snaplen / > orig_len, bad version, pcapng block-length mismatch; \"which capture is malformed\" | gap (pcap-malformed-integrity) | record walk ends short of EOF; trailing bytes | struct | high (D27 flavor \"reject malformed captures\") |\n| 176 | Network EXPORTS: Zeek TSV/JSON logs, Suricata eve.json, NetFlow v5/v9/IPFIX, Wireshark CSV, W3C firewall logs (`pfirewall.log`) | gap (network-flow-log-exports) | `#separator \\\\x09` + `#fields`; `\"event_type\":`; u16 version 5/9/10 @0; `#Fields:` | stdlib text/struct | high (D27 flavor \"exports\") |\n| 177 | Host network evidence: Sysmon EID 3 NetworkConnect / 22 DNSEvent, netstat/ipconfig text, hosts file, DNS cache; host-claim vs capture join | gap (host-network-evidence, host-vs-network-synthesis) | EVTX Sysmon channel; `Proto  Local Address` header | evtx_binxml (built) + text parsers | high (D27 flavor \"host narrative missing network evidence\") |\n| 178 | Capture-format zoo: snoop, NetMon `GMBU`, ERF, Kuznetzov `a1b2cd34`, pktmon/netsh `.etl`, gz-wrapped pcap; HAR JSON | gap (capture-format-zoo, har-json-capture) | `snoop\\\\0\\\\0\\\\0`; `GMBU`; `{\"log\":{\"version\"` | struct / json | med |\n| 179 | Cloud / identity audit logs: M365 Unified Audit Log CSV/JSON, Entra sign-ins, AWS CloudTrail `Records[]`, Okta System Log | gap (cloud-identity-audit-logs) | `\"eventVersion\"`+`\"eventSource\"`; `CreationDate,UserIds,Operations,AuditData` | json / csv text | low-med (Huntress ITDR theme) |\"\"\"+t[j:]\n# cue line\nold=\"d4 c3 b2 a1 / a1 b2 c3 d4 / 0a 0d 0d 0a  PCAP/PCAPNG  linktype u32 @20; capinfos -M; dpkt\"\nnew=\"d4 c3 b2 a1 LE-us / 4d 3c b2 a1 LE-ns / a1 b2 c3 d4 BE / 0a 0d 0d 0a pcapng: PCAP (D27 `pcap.packet_count` = walk 16-B rec hdrs by incl_len@+8 from 24; order FROM MAGIC; snapped recs count); pcapng EPB6/SPB3/OPB2\"\nrep(old,new)\n# gaps\ni=t.index('## Readiness gaps'); j=t.index('```json',i); k=t.index('```',j+7)\ng=json.loads(t[j+7:k])\ng=[x for x in g if x['id']!='pcap-header']\nby={x['id']:x for x in g}\nby['synthesis-siblings']['detail']+=\" D27: SIX names (note/png/msi/wav/jar/pcap, order shuffled per set) in TT and all 11 Mastery sets, still sha256 -- the list length grows; parse it, never count it.\"\nby['timed-carryover-mutations']['detail']+=\" D27: TT 32 / Mastery 352 (11 sets) first try with zero generalize; the new pcap family already mutated within classic libpcap in the timed sets (LE-us, LE-ns 4d3cb2a1, BE a1b2c3d4; linktypes 1/101/105/147; snapped records). From D28 the kit carries d27-pcap-001-pcap-packet-count -- see pcap-carryover-variants.\"\nfor x in g:\n    if x['id'] in ('ese-edb-header','amcache-shimcache','usn-journal-records','recycle-bin-i','jumplist','mft-record','ntfs-boot-sector-vbr'):\n        x['priority']=2\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"pcap-carryover-variants\",\"concept\":\"PCAP as a CARRIED timed family: every container the D28+ kits may mutate capture-001.pcap into\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Harden lib/meta/prebuilt/pcap.py packet_count (and every pcap field) for: pcapng (SHB 0a0d0d0a with BOM 1a2b3c4d either order, MULTIPLE sections each re-setting byte order, count EPB 6 + SPB 3 + obsolete PB 2 only -- not IDB/ISB/NRB/DSB/custom 0x0bad/0x40000bad), Kuznetzov modified pcap magic a1b2cd34 (24-B record header: +ifindex u32, protocol u16, pkt_type u8, pad), nanosecond a1b23c4d in both orders, IXIA/AIX variants (a1b2c3d4 with version 2.2/2.3), a truncated tail record (not counted, capinfos behaviour), zero-length records (counted), gzip-wrapped `.pcap.gz` (1f 8b -> decompress then parse). Fixtures: each magic x each byte order, pcapng with 2 sections + 2 IDBs, a 1-byte-short tail. Fields stay packet_count / linktype / snaplen / first/last_packet_time_utc.\"},\n {\"id\":\"pcap-malformed-integrity\",\"concept\":\"Malformed-capture detection ('reject malformed captures', D27 flavor)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"New module lib/meta/prebuilt/pcap_integrity.py (pure struct, reuse pcap.py parse). fmt pcap/pcapng fields: is_malformed / is_valid (enum true|false), malformed_reason (enum-ish: truncated_record, incl_len_exceeds_snaplen, incl_len_exceeds_orig_len, bad_magic, bad_version, block_length_mismatch, trailing_bytes), truncated_record_count, trailing_bytes_count (bytes after the last complete record), complete_record_count, declared_vs_walked mismatch for pcapng ISB isb_ifrecv/isb_ifdrop, records_exceeding_snaplen_count, non_monotonic_timestamp_count, max_incl_len. Synthesis shapes: '*-malformed-capture-names' / 'which of Files is malformed' -> JSON sorted list of member names whose walk fails; 'valid capture count'. Never raise: a malformed file must still answer packet_count = complete records.\"},\n {\"id\":\"pcap-l3l4-decode\",\"concept\":\"Packet decode L2-L4: unique IPs, conversations, ports, protocol counts, byte totals\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"New module lib/meta/prebuilt/pcap_flows.py (stdlib struct only; dpkt is not gate-allowed). Decode per linktype: 1 Ethernet (+802.1Q/QinQ 8100/88a8, ethertype 0800/86dd/0806), 0 NULL/BSD loopback (u32 AF host order), 101/12/14 raw IP, 113 Linux SLL (16 B), 276 SLL2 (20 B), 105 802.11 + 127 radiotap (LLC/SNAP), 228/229 raw IPv4/IPv6; skip 147-162 USER* (count only). IPv4 IHL, IPv6 next-header chain, TCP data offset, UDP. Fields (fmt pcap, also pcapng): unique_ip_count, unique_src_ips / unique_dst_ips (sorted JSON), top_talker_ip (most packets, tie -> lowest), conversation_count (unordered IP pair) and flow_count (5-tuple, unordered), tcp_packet_count, udp_packet_count, icmp_packet_count, arp_packet_count, ipv6_packet_count, protocol_counts (JSON object?), dst_ports (sorted ints), total_bytes (sum orig_len) vs captured_bytes (sum incl_len), tcp_syn_count, capture_duration_seconds, most_common_dst_port. Spellings: IPs dotted / RFC 5952 compressed IPv6 lowercase.\"},\n {\"id\":\"pcap-app-indicators\",\"concept\":\"Application-layer indicators from captures: DNS, HTTP, TLS SNI, FTP/SMTP creds\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Builds on pcap-l3l4-decode (import its walker). DNS over UDP/53 (and TCP/53 length-prefixed): query names (label decode with compression pointers, lowercase, no trailing dot), qtypes, answer A/AAAA/CNAME values, rcode NXDOMAIN count -> dns_query_names (sorted unique JSON), dns_answer_ips, most_queried_domain. HTTP/1.x on any TCP payload starting with a method token: methods, Host, request URIs, User-Agent, response status codes, Content-Type; first request URL = http://Host+URI. TLS: ClientHello (handshake type 1) SNI extension 0, ALPN 16, version; Certificate (TLS<=1.2) DER -> hand to x509 module (sha256 fingerprint, subject CN). Optional JA3 (md5 of version,ciphers,extensions,curves,formats; GREASE removed). FTP USER/PASS, SMTP MAIL FROM/RCPT TO, ICMP payload strings. Fields: dns_query_names, http_hosts, http_user_agents, http_request_uris, tls_sni_names, tls_ja3_md5, ftp_usernames, smtp_mail_from -- all lists sorted+deduped; *_first / *_count variants.\"},\n {\"id\":\"network-flow-log-exports\",\"concept\":\"Network EXPORTS beside a capture: Zeek, Suricata eve.json, NetFlow v5/v9/IPFIX, Wireshark CSV, W3C firewall logs\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D27 flavor: 'Packet captures, exports, and host artifacts'. New module lib/meta/prebuilt/netlogs.py (stdlib, no csv module if gate forbids -> manual split). fmt zeek (aliases bro, conn_log, dns_log, http_log): TSV with `#separator \\\\x09`, `#fields` and `#types` headers, `#close`; or JSON-lines -> record_count, unique uids, id.orig_h/id.resp_h sets, service set, total orig_bytes/resp_bytes, dns query set, http host set. fmt suricata (eve, eve_json): JSON lines event_type alert/dns/http/tls/flow -> alert_signatures (sorted), alert_count, signature_ids, src/dest ips. fmt netflow: v5 header (version u16 BE =5 @0, count u16 @2, sys_uptime, unix_secs @8) + 48-B records (srcaddr, dstaddr, nexthop, input, output, dPkts, dOctets, first, last, srcport, dstport, tcp_flags, prot) -> record_count, total_packets (sum dPkts), total_bytes, unique dst; v9/IPFIX (version 9/10) template flowsets -> record_count via templates. fmt csv_flows (Wireshark 'Export Packet Dissections as CSV': \\\"No.\\\",\\\"Time\\\",\\\"Source\\\",\\\"Destination\\\",\\\"Protocol\\\",\\\"Length\\\",\\\"Info\\\") -> row_count, protocols. fmt firewall_log (pfirewall.log W3C `#Fields: date time action protocol src-ip dst-ip src-port dst-port size ...`) -> drop_count, allow_count, unique dst. Cross-check field: export count vs capture packet_count disagreement.\"},\n {\"id\":\"host-network-evidence\",\"concept\":\"Host artifacts that narrate network activity: Sysmon EID 3/22, netstat/ipconfig text, hosts file, DNS client cache, RDP/VPN logs\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D27 flavor: 'find the host narrative missing network evidence'. New module lib/meta/prebuilt/host_net.py. EVTX path: reuse evtx_binxml (built) to read Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational EID 3 (Image, Protocol, SourceIp, SourcePort, DestinationIp, DestinationHostname, DestinationPort, UtcTime) and EID 22 (QueryName, QueryResults, Image); Security 5156 WFP (Application, DestAddress, DestPort); TerminalServices 1149 (source IP). Text paths: `netstat -ano` (Proto Local Address Foreign Address State PID) -> established remote endpoints; `ipconfig /displaydns` (Record Name / A (Host) Record); hosts file non-comment mappings; bash/zsh history ssh/curl/wget/nc targets. Fields: remote_ips (sorted), remote_endpoints (`ip:port` sorted), dns_query_names, connecting_images (process paths), connection_count, first_connection_time_utc.\"},\n {\"id\":\"host-vs-network-synthesis\",\"concept\":\"Cross-member join: host claims vs capture traffic (the claim with no matching packets)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"New lib/meta/prebuilt/synthesis_network.py using pcap-l3l4-decode + host-network-evidence + network-flow-log-exports. Given Files [capture(s), host logs, exports]: build the capture's (dst ip, dst port, proto) set and DNS names; for each host claim (Sysmon EID3 / netstat / firewall allow / Zeek conn row) test presence -> answers: host_claims_missing_network_evidence (JSON sorted `ip:port` or member name of the host artifact whose narrative has no packets), capture_without_host_evidence, matched_claim_count, the HOSTNAME/member that lies. Also 'which capture is malformed' (via pcap-malformed-integrity) and 'total packets across valid captures'. Id guess: metadata-day-NN-synthesis-<what> or dNN-<fmt>-NNN-...-missing-*; dispatch on any id containing missing|unmatched|without|orphan.\"},\n {\"id\":\"capture-format-zoo\",\"concept\":\"Non-libpcap capture formats and wrappers: snoop, NetMon, ERF, pktmon/netsh ETL, gz-wrapped\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Extend pcap packet_count/linktype to: Solaris snoop (`snoop\\\\0\\\\0\\\\0` @0, version u32 BE @8, datalink u32 @12; records orig_len u32, incl_len u32, record_len u32 (padded), drops, ts sec/usec -> walk by record_len), Microsoft Network Monitor 2.x (`GMBU` @0, ver @4/@5, mac type u16 @6, frame table offset u32 @0x18 / length @0x1c -> frame count = len/4), NetMon 1.x (`RTSS`), Endace ERF (no magic: 16-B record hdr ts u64, type u8, flags, rlen u16 BE, lctr, wlen -> walk by rlen), pcap-in-gzip (1f 8b), Windows pktmon/netsh trace .etl (event count via the built etl module; pktmon PacketFragment events). fmt words pcap/capture/snoop/netmon/erf. An unknown magic -> 'none' (do not guess a count).\"},\n {\"id\":\"har-json-capture\",\"concept\":\"HAR 1.2 HTTP archive exports (browser 'save as HAR')\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"fmt har: JSON {log:{version, creator{name,version}, browser, pages[], entries[]}} -> entry_count, page_count, creator_name, creator_version, request_urls (sorted unique), request_methods, response_status_codes, server_ip_addresses (entries[].serverIPAddress), first_request_url (by startedDateTime ISO), hosts (from URL netloc), mime types, total response bodySize (skip -1), cookies names. Web lane overlaps (it also parses HAR) -- keep pure json/urllib.parse.\"},\n {\"id\":\"tls-certs-in-capture\",\"concept\":\"Certificates and TLS fingerprints carried inside captures; SSLKEYLOGFILE\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"From pcap-app-indicators TLS reassembly (TCP segments of one stream in seq order): Certificate handshake (type 11, TLS<=1.2) -> leaf DER -> reuse prebuilt x509 (subject_cn, issuer_cn, serial_hex, not_after_utc, sha256_fingerprint); server_cert_fingerprints (sorted); JA3/JA3S md5; ServerHello chosen cipher hex `0x%04x`. fmt sslkeylog (text `CLIENT_RANDOM <64 hex> <96 hex>` / TLS1.3 `CLIENT_HANDSHAKE_TRAFFIC_SECRET`) -> line_count, client_randoms, label set; pcapng DSB (block type 0x0000000A, secrets type 0x544c534b 'TLSK') -> embedded keylog.\"},\n {\"id\":\"cloud-identity-audit-logs\",\"concept\":\"Cloud / identity audit exports: M365 Unified Audit Log, Entra sign-in logs, AWS CloudTrail, Okta System Log\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"On-brand for Huntress ITDR; plausible 'host/identity narrative' artifact in the last days. fmt ual (aliases m365_audit, unified_audit_log): CSV CreationDate,UserIds,Operations,AuditData(JSON string) -> record_count, operations (sorted unique), user_ids, client_ips (AuditData.ClientIP / ActorIpAddress), first/last CreationDate; MailItemsAccessed / New-InboxRule names. fmt entra_signin (JSON array or CSV): userPrincipalName, ipAddress, appDisplayName, status.errorCode, location -> failed_signin_count, ip set. fmt cloudtrail: {\\\"Records\\\":[{eventVersion,eventTime,eventSource,eventName,awsRegion,sourceIPAddress,userIdentity{type,arn,userName}}]} (also gz) -> record_count, event_names (sorted unique), source_ips, regions, first_event_time_utc. fmt okta (System Log JSON: eventType, actor.alternateId, client.ipAddress, outcome.result). Pure json; manual CSV split honouring quotes.\"},\n]\ng.extend(new)\norder={1:0,2:1,3:2}\ng.sort(key=lambda x:x['priority'])  # stable within priority\nblob=\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False) for x in g)+\"\\n]\"\njson.loads(blob)\nt=t[:j+7]+\"\\n\"+blob+\"\\n\"+t[k:]\n# ranking prose\na=t.index(\"Ranking (D26 post-run)\"); b=t.index(\"TARGETS-style `fmt`/`fields` given in `detail`\")\nt=t[:a]+\"\"\"Ranking (D27 post-run): priority 1 = plausible D28-D30 question with no extractor or a lane-wide failure mode.\nD27 left the WINDOWS DFIR block (D24-26) for NETWORK evidence (`pcap.packet_count`, fmt = file-format word). Its flavor\nnames three angles -- captures, EXPORTS, HOST artifacts -- plus \"reject malformed captures\" and \"host narrative\nmissing network evidence\", so priority 1 = making the newly carried pcap family survive timed mutation (pcapng,\nKuznetzov, truncated tail), malformed-capture detection, packet decode (flows, DNS/HTTP/TLS), flow-log exports\n(Zeek/Suricata/NetFlow/firewall) and host network evidence + the host-vs-capture join. Unbuilt Windows text DFIR,\nLinux DFIR, HAR, capture-format zoo and cloud/identity audit logs at 2; certs-in-capture at 3. The built D24-26 DFIR\npriority-1 items moved to 2 (built; the prebuild drains only unbuilt `prebuild` gaps).\n\"\"\"+t[b:]\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\nPYEOF\npython3 $TMPDIR/ed_cov.py && echo ok"}}}
